WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.516 --> 00:00:04.340
- One time my (beeping) mom said,

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.460
she said, I was telling her
like what I wanted to do.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.980
I was like right out of high school

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.620
or still in high school
and I told her I wanted

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.070
to be a music video director

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.297
because back then in the 90's

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:17.120
that was all the rage, music videos

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.953
and when I was telling her I wanted

00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:19.670
to go to LA and like study film

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.433
and do all this stuff and
make videos for musicians,

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:27.203
she said, "Oh, people like
us don't make it like that."

00:00:27.203 --> 00:00:30.030
Say, we're not successful in that way,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:34.530
we don't make it that far up
in life and that destroyed me,

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:39.010
that just (beeping) totally
flattened my dreams,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.843
aspirations,

00:00:39.843 --> 00:00:40.890
whatever you wanna call them.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.710
I internalized it, (beeping)
myself up and it became true,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.904
here I am.

00:00:45.904 --> 00:00:46.737
That's it.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:48.792
That's what hurt.

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:49.625
It's hurt the most,

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:51.510
it was the most hurtful
thing that we can't make it.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.385
I can (beeping) make it,
maybe you can't make it.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:54.719
I can make it.

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:55.940
- [Friend] You should
have told your mom that.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.650
- I should have (beeping)
told her that, but I didn't.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.023
I made it come true.

00:01:00.202 --> 00:01:01.035
- [Thoraya] Well, you can make it,

00:01:01.035 --> 00:01:01.869
and you could still make it.

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:03.301
Have you thought about that?

00:01:03.301 --> 00:01:05.032
- It's a lot of work.

00:01:05.032 --> 00:01:06.340
It's a lot of work.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.040
I don't want to, maybe
that's what she meant,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.820
we're too lazy to do that.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.980
Maybe that's what she meant.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.263
Ultimately she was right.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.800
- Was something that my sister said

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.383
to me or asked me actually,
it was a question.

00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:22.890
She asked me why she had down syndrome

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.820
and why I did not and I think it was sad

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.570
because I had no idea how to answer

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.950
'cause yeah, I'm still working
in my head through that one.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.930
Why we're born certain ways.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.428
I think it's something I'll
probably always deal with

00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:43.428
but I think I'm definitely
healing guilt or healing, yeah,

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.050
that feeling of guilt that I have

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.530
for things that predate me

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.160
'cause she's older than me and also

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.960
that it had nothing to do with me.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.883
I'm just a bystander.

00:01:53.841 --> 00:01:54.720
- I don't know.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.900
My mom says all kinds of painful things.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:01.900
Probably like I regret
having you, probably that.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.963
For me, I always remind myself

00:02:05.963 --> 00:02:10.065
that it must be harder to be her

00:02:10.065 --> 00:02:13.197
than it is to be around her.

00:02:13.197 --> 00:02:16.549
So I try and have empathy
and compassion for that

00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:18.533
but if I was her and I was going

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:21.040
through what she goes
through and I struggle

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.593
with what she struggles with that I would,

00:02:22.593 --> 00:02:24.610
that it would be hard for me too

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.409
and I would have moments
where I made mistakes.

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:29.860
So that's how I get through it.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:34.860
- I was a lad and doing my usual show off,

00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:37.008
talk all the time routine,

00:02:37.008 --> 00:02:41.180
looking for attention
and I got the attention

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.730
from a couple of girls who weren't

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.730
into me and one of them said,
"Do you have an off button?"

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.697
And that struck me, cut me to the quick.

00:02:53.697 --> 00:02:54.910
Now it's a joke.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.270
I've layered it over.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.224
It's a pearl now, not a grain of sand.

00:02:58.224 --> 00:03:03.224
- That my mom actually asked my dad

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.650
to get me and my two siblings

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.578
versus my dad taking
us on his own volition.

00:03:10.578 --> 00:03:11.411
- [Friend] Hmm.

00:03:11.411 --> 00:03:12.700
- Yeah.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:16.711
Basically being told that my
mom no longer wanted her kids.

00:03:16.711 --> 00:03:17.990
- [Friend] I didn't know that.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:19.520
- Yeah, 'cause I had been living

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.520
with this narrative that my
dad saved us which he did.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.530
He still did but he did it partially

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:33.530
because he was prompted to
do it, you know what I mean?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.783
- [Thoraya] Hmm, does it still hurt?

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:44.140
- No, because I'm so grateful

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.540
for my dad for doing
that and I'm where I am

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.403
and who I am because my
dad saved us essentially.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.160
- My ex-boyfriend told me I was abusive

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.470
and I've been doing a
lot of reflection on it.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.740
I think that really he was the abusive one

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:04.665
and it was very hurtful

00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:09.665
'cause it makes me overthink
every single thing I do

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.380
or say to anybody now.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:15.304
So it's kind of like his
abuse did really mentally

00:04:15.304 --> 00:04:18.323
(beeping) with me and
that (beeping) hurts.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.700
- Yeah, I remember when I was younger,

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.610
my grandparents basically
saying like, you know,

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.540
if you're gay, we will still love you

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.980
but we won't associate with
you and we'll disown you.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.778
So I've always remembered that

00:04:31.778 --> 00:04:33.924
and that is something that I've kind

00:04:33.924 --> 00:04:37.884
of haven't been able
to let go just yet, so.

00:04:37.884 --> 00:04:42.333
- The most hurtful thing that
somebody say to me is like,

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.540
they were ashamed to be with me

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.923
because I am not the
person that I used to be.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.660
- I was dating this guy and he told me

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.760
that he wouldn't introduce me

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.343
to his mom until I lost weight.

00:04:58.199 --> 00:05:01.114
- Being told that you are too much

00:05:01.114 --> 00:05:02.900
is probably the most hurtful thing

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.120
anyone has ever said to me.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:07.200
- That I wasn't worthy of love.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.349
- That you deserve the world

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:10.626
but I don't know how to give it to you.

00:05:10.626 --> 00:05:13.493
- Ooh, I don't even wanna say it out loud.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.883
That being with anyone
after their ex felt wrong.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.000
It was in a different context.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.140
It was actually after we dated

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.700
when we were friends and they just kind

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.543
of said it without thinking

00:05:27.543 --> 00:05:30.310
but we dated after he broke up

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.960
with an ex who he's like real in love

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.730
with and said being with anyone

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.300
after her just like didn't feel right.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.343
It felt fake and I was like,
oh (beeping), cool, yeah.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.720
- It was when I was a sophomore

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.460
in high school and I was hanging out

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.757
with my grandma who's
Cambodian and I had really,

00:05:46.757 --> 00:05:49.930
really long hair at the time
I had like waist length hair,

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.975
it had always been kind
of a big deal to me

00:05:51.975 --> 00:05:54.500
and I wanted to cut it
and I was telling her

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.300
about my plans to get it cut pretty short

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.197
and I have pretty short hair now

00:05:57.197 --> 00:05:58.573
and I've had it short since then

00:05:58.573 --> 00:06:01.852
but she asked me if I had asked my dad

00:06:01.852 --> 00:06:04.969
for permission to get it
cut which was something

00:06:04.969 --> 00:06:07.050
that I had kind of just
brushed off as like, ah,

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.131
classic grandma pulling an
old like patriarchy thing

00:06:10.131 --> 00:06:14.240
but as I've continued to mull that over,

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.360
it has been something that I return

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.085
to a lot of thinking about my own, like,

00:06:20.085 --> 00:06:22.347
I don't know, existence, upbringing,

00:06:22.347 --> 00:06:25.854
development, et cetera, so yeah.

00:06:25.854 --> 00:06:29.410
- I would say the most
hurtful thing I've been told

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.320
was I'm never gonna be anything.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.710
Like I won't accomplish
anything in my life.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.700
I almost believed it.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.367
Like I felt like they knew.

00:06:40.367 --> 00:06:42.430
So it was kind of one

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:45.790
of those things I had
to overcome growing up.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.120
- [Thoraya] And did you prove them wrong?

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.150
- Oh, definitely.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.150
I'm doing great now.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.391
- Someone told me that they
hope that my wedding sucks.

00:06:55.391 --> 00:06:57.363
- [Thoraya] Did you have your wedding yet?

00:06:57.363 --> 00:06:58.902
- Yes, it was yesterday.

00:06:58.902 --> 00:06:59.815
- [Thoraya] It was?

00:06:59.815 --> 00:07:00.950
- Yeah.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:01.783
- [Thoraya] And how was it?

00:07:01.783 --> 00:07:03.300
- It was amazing.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.528
- I had an ex boyfriend one time

00:07:04.528 --> 00:07:05.960
who was talking about

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.850
how like conventionally
attractive he thought he was,

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:12.630
I guess and he says to
me, he's like, well,

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.080
you're not conventionally beautiful.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.735
It sticks with me, like, you know,

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:19.794
as a Thoraya you are thinking about how,

00:07:19.794 --> 00:07:23.740
you're thinking about
beauty standards a lot

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.362
and I always come back to that like,

00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.187
well, I'm not conventionally beautiful.

00:07:27.187 --> 00:07:28.811
So I have to work my other,

00:07:28.811 --> 00:07:33.480
my unconventionally attractive qualities,

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.495
I suppose, you know?

00:07:34.495 --> 00:07:37.100
- I think it was also because

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.410
of the person that told it to me

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.200
who was someone that I thought
really knew me really well,

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.616
but he told me that I don't have dreams

00:07:43.616 --> 00:07:46.550
and I was so offended by that

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.820
because I have such big dreams

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.100
and this person that knew
me so well I thought,

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:55.690
thought this of me and I was shocked.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:57.173
I was flabbergasted.

00:07:57.173 --> 00:07:58.950
- So the most hurtful thing

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.420
that I've ever been told was the reason

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:06.160
why I got cheated on and it
was because I was too sad.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.921
I really felt like betrayed
and like really hurt

00:08:09.921 --> 00:08:11.124
'cause it's like, you know,

00:08:11.124 --> 00:08:13.280
this was like my partner and it was like,

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.975
you know, when I needed you the most like,

00:08:14.975 --> 00:08:19.080
you cheat on me and like
do that while I was sad,

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.700
like I was depressed like
this, I was depressed.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.673
So like, it (beeping) me up.

00:08:24.665 --> 00:08:28.340
- I reached out to an ex of mine

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.210
before I was having a surgery,

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:32.760
just to be like, hey,
before I go through with it,

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.130
I just wanted you to know that I care

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:35.399
about you and just kind

00:08:35.399 --> 00:08:40.253
of like said some kind things
and she responded by saying,

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.138
I have a partner right now

00:08:42.138 --> 00:08:43.341
and we both don't feel comfortable

00:08:43.341 --> 00:08:48.341
with you contacting me
and that hurt my feelings.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:51.640
Sometimes I still feel
the pain when I think

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.820
about it as compared to other things

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:55.800
that might have been painful,

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.760
that don't really resonate as pain now.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.599
- So mine was like, when I was struggling

00:09:01.599 --> 00:09:04.670
with eating and like just my body image

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.680
in general and I went to Italy

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.020
which is like where I'm from

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.870
and I was in a bathing suit and like,

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.330
I already wasn't feeling that great

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.995
and then my grandma like
looked at me and she's like,

00:09:14.995 --> 00:09:16.591
damn, like, you'd be perfect

00:09:16.591 --> 00:09:18.740
if you lost some weight and like

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.201
that just kind of hit 'cause it was like,

00:09:20.201 --> 00:09:22.045
like that's what I was trying,

00:09:22.045 --> 00:09:24.350
or not trying to do, I was trying to like,

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.730
accept myself for who I
was and then her saying

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:31.300
that was like, you need
to be better and yeah.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.831
So that was my most painful thing.

00:09:33.831 --> 00:09:36.810
- I think one anecdote

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:39.933
that sticks out is one time
I was in the parking lot

00:09:39.933 --> 00:09:41.860
with my mom when I was in high school

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:43.390
and I'm a junior in college now,

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.920
I don't remember exactly when
this happened and I was like,

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.184
hey mom, I think maybe

00:09:47.184 --> 00:09:48.941
that I have like social anxiety

00:09:48.941 --> 00:09:51.115
and I didn't really think anything of it,

00:09:51.115 --> 00:09:54.560
I thought she would be
like ask me questions

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.656
about it because we have a
pretty close relationship

00:09:56.656 --> 00:09:59.730
but she said like, oh, I hope not,

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.710
like don't turn out to be weird

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.480
or something like that and I was like, oh,

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.740
okay, I will not bring this up

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:08.060
with you further and
then it made me hesitant

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.160
to like further explore it
when I was in high school

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.410
which probably would have
been helpful given me having

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.110
difficulties with socializing with people

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:18.480
in high school, so yeah.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.470
- The most painful thing I remember

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:24.490
that sort of just like
hurt me in a way was like,

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.366
when I told my mom

00:10:25.366 --> 00:10:29.460
that I felt like I
couldn't like live anymore.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.970
Like I don't wanna do this anymore,

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:32.840
like I just can't do it and
I started like telling her

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.310
about like things that happened in my past

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:35.610
that she just like didn't know about.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.767
The thing that like hurt
me where she was like,

00:10:36.767 --> 00:10:39.037
"You were meant to go through that stuff."

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:41.460
It was like to make you stronger

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.680
but it just made me feel a lot weaker

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.650
because I feel like I wanted
to be a normal person.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.364
It just hurt to hear that my mom, like,

00:10:47.364 --> 00:10:48.887
it almost felt like she cared,

00:10:48.887 --> 00:10:51.040
but like she cared in like the wrong way.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:51.980
This is like the first time I was like

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.020
actually truthful with her.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.510
So like, it like hurt me
to hear that she was like,

00:10:55.510 --> 00:11:00.510
it's for the best that you
were like very much destroyed

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.937
in a way, like as a child

00:11:01.937 --> 00:11:06.663
and I guess it's like the
most painful thing I've heard.

